<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Cavia porcellus Holocene (0 Ma) Turing wavelength at 126.7 µm (tier-5 detail s0) (Cavia porcellus (Guinea pig), I. Enaima (Vertebrata) -> Mammalia (Zootoka) -> Cavia)",
        "Cavia porcellus Holocene (0 Ma) Turing wavelength at 126.7 µm (tier-5 detail s0) faithfully reproduces Cavia porcellus (Guinea pig), I. Enaima (Vertebrata) -> Mammalia (Zootoka) -> Cavia morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Cavia porcellus (Guinea pig), I. Enaima (Vertebrata) -> Mammalia (Zootoka) -> Cavia specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Cavia porcellus (Guinea pig), I. Enaima (Vertebrata) -> Mammalia (Zootoka) -> Cavia" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A full nonlinear two-species Schnakenberg integration. The rendered field is the Swift-Hohenberg amplitude equation.",
        "does_not_claim: Machine execution of the Lean file: this image has no lean binary.",
        "does_not_claim: That the gallery pigment field is a published micrograph, or that its measured dominant wavelength (78.18 µm on the printed 100 µm bar) equals 126.7 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian at a = 0.08, b = 1.15, gamma = 1, with D_v/D_u = 40 scaled so lambda_c = 126.7 µm exactly (D_u = 169.175 µm^2, D_v = 6767.013 µm^2).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Swift-Hohenberg spiral of charge 2 on a periodic 1.0136 mm window (eight critical wavelengths), plus an epsilon sweep, a below-onset decay, and a plain-diffusion ablation.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray (1981) identified that selected wavelength with mammalian coat stripes and spots. Schnakenberg (1979) supplied the activator-substrate kinetics used here.",
        "reported_in_source: Sick et al. (2006) showed a WNT/DKK reaction-diffusion interaction sets mammalian hair-follicle spacing, the anatomical neighbour of a ~100 µm pigment wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Swift & Hohenberg (1977) and Cross & Hohenberg (1993) give the real amplitude equation whose linear spectrum peaks at a prescribed k_c.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion: a homogeneous steady state stable to k = 0 can be unstable at a finite critical wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses farther than the activator.",
        "transfer_boundary: 126.7 µm is the slot-assigned tier-5 detail length (0.0001267 m, log10 = -3.897) for extant Cavia porcellus at 0 Ma, not a measurement quoted from a guinea-pig histology paper.",
        "transfer_boundary: The Cavia chronoseries has one node. The 1267 µm and 12.67 µm neighbours are adjacent size tiers at the same age, not other chronospecies." ;
